{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans","id":1127764,"title":"Great news for Lunar fans!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-11T13:35:33-07:00","id":1127764,"title":"Great news for Lunar fans!","content":"From rpg.net<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Demented One</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jurgen Hubert</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">AFAIK Exigents will come before Lunars anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the original plan, but for a number of reasons - like, &quot;Lunars are really cool and people love them&quot; - we've moved Lunars up ahead of Exigents. Eric Minton and I are currently working on the outline for their book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that means it's very possible Lunars could be out in 2018!<br /> <br /> After DB, this is the book my playgroup most wants/needs, so having both of those would go a long way to making Exalted 3rd edition feel like a full game.<br /> <br /> It might even make me want to run Exalted again!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T13:43:21-07:00","id":1127769,"title":"","content":"I am so happy about this. As in... while my playgroup enjoys Solars, I think we all really, really want Lunars. So... yeah. Now, please excuse me while I go dance around the house.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T13:48:46-07:00","id":1127772,"title":"","content":"Quite a reasonable reaction!<br /> <br /> Yeah, my players are mostly (but not entirely) happy to play Solars, but a fair few prefer playing Lunars.<br /> Actually, in my 3rd ed game, there were 5 Solars and 2 Lunars (which, obviously, didn't work brilliantly, mechanics-wise) and in the game I play, we have 3 Solars, a Lunar and a Fair Folk. And I'm only playing a Solar because it's too much hassle to play anything else. I'd much rather play a Lunar (I did play one, but I retired him when we switched to 3rd ed).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T13:54:36-07:00","id":1127773,"title":"","content":"Well that makes sense. Lunars are far more important to the setting in terms of impact, history and relationship dynamic with the already published exalts (they are the DBs number one foe officially and have the weird relationship dynamic with the Solars).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T13:59:40-07:00","id":1127776,"title":"","content":"Very cool! I'm dying to see what the new Lunars can do in this edition - I'm really hoping they're better than in 1e and 2e, very excited!<br /> <br /> On the other hand... Exigents was a tremendously important book, because it helped everyone create charms <i>of any kind</i>. As an ST, I'll need to be able to craft half-decent charms for my QCs and NPCs in general if I don't want every one of them to eventually start feeling a bit of the same (been there, done that). I really hope we get Exigents very soon after!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T14:20:34-07:00","id":1127781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1127773#post1127773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that makes sense. Lunars are far more important to the setting in terms of impact, history and relationship dynamic with the already published exalts (they are the DBs number one foe officially and have the weird relationship dynamic with the Solars).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, definitely. They're a major part of the setting. Arguably more so than Solars, as they've been around for ages.<br /> Definitely more than Exigents, especially as it was said that there aren't actually that many Exigents around.<br /> <br /> I think this is probably a good business decision as well, as it's probably easier to get back old players who played 1st or 2nd ed but haven't bought 3rd, with a fresh new vision of a fan-favourite splat rather than something entirely new.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T14:30:06-07:00","id":1127784,"title":"","content":"I dunno, as someone who's attempting to flesh out a completely new exalt concept and simultaneously attempt to flesh out a playable/ usable alchemical charm set I kinda feel like those guidelines could have been really handy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T15:37:21-07:00","id":1127801,"title":"","content":"I am glad that they will be coming through with Lunar, though I hope that they do a better job than 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T15:47:46-07:00","id":1127804,"title":"","content":"Revised release order guess<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded<br /> Lunars<br /> Exigents<br /> Sidereals<br /> Getimians<br /> Abyssals<br /> Liminals<br /> Infernals<br /> ???<br /> Alchemicals<br /> ???<br /> ???","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T15:54:59-07:00","id":1127808,"title":"","content":"I actually expect Abyssals before Sidereals, but honestly, it probably depends how inspired the Devs are feeling about one or the other.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T16:16:32-07:00","id":1127815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1127808#post1127808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually expect Abyssals before Sidereals, but honestly, it probably depends how inspired the Devs are feeling about one or the other.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I hope not. Sidereals are more of a setting pillar involved in core conflicts of other major pillar splats. Abyssals (while no less awesome if done right) are a new X factor to the setting (in universe I mean, not that they're new to third edition) far less automatically entwined with the built in conflicts of Lunars, Solars, and Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T16:18:56-07:00","id":1127818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1127815#post1127815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope not. Sidereals are more of a setting pillar involved in core conflicts of other major pillar splats. Abyssals (while no less awesome if done right) are a new X factor to the setting (in universe I mean, not that they're new to third edition) far less automatically entwined with the built in conflicts of Lunars, Solars, and Dragon-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>While a legitimate point, historically Abyssals have always come out before Sidereals, hence the expectation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T16:38:17-07:00","id":1127822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1127776#post1127776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very cool! I'm dying to see what the new Lunars can do in this edition - I'm really hoping they're better than in 1e and 2e, very excited!<br /> <br /> On the other hand... Exigents was a tremendously important book, because it helped everyone create charms <i>of any kind</i>. As an ST, I'll need to be able to craft half-decent charms for my QCs and NPCs in general if I don't want every one of them to eventually start feeling a bit of the same (been there, done that). I really hope we get Exigents very soon after!</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely we have higher expectations than just &quot;better than 1e and 2e&quot;, or even &quot;better than 1e and 2e combined&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T17:36:53-07:00","id":1127846,"title":"","content":"I have to admit I'm quite happy about this. The material in the core and dev/writer discussions so far have suggested that Third Edition has a very strong and cohesive thesis for Lunars, and I can't wait to see that realized sooner rather than later.<br /> <br /> Exigents should be a jewel to homebrew and provide a flood of content, but those objectives are what's likely to make it a very hard book to write. So it's understandable in terms of design that Lunars would be made first, contributing to a solid picture of exalted mechanics in Ex3 to build on with something as flexible and ambitious as a book on making your own exalts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 08-11-2017, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T17:37:29-07:00","id":1127848,"title":"","content":"This is a pretty good decsion-- as people have said, the fact is that the Lunars are, arguably as involved with the setting as the Dragonblooded are. Y ou may or may not meet abyssals or Getimen, but no matter where a solar is in creation, he or she is probably going to run into either a Lunar aligned faction or a Dragonblooded aligned faction.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T17:38:54-07:00","id":1127849,"title":"","content":"My love for Lunars is possibly distorting my judgement , but I think the authors having another set of charms behind them prior to doing the Exigent book can only be a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","user":"Apromor","date":". 08-11-2017, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T17:48:08-07:00","id":1127857,"title":"","content":"Very good news. As far as I'm concerned, all the new types should be moved to the end of the release schedule. While perhaps more interesting as thought exercises in new types of Exalts, the 3rd Edition additional types can really wait until when/if the older established Exalts become officially playable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T19:56:36-07:00","id":1127893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1127804#post1127804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon-Blooded<br /> Lunars<br /> Exigents<br /> Sidereals<br /> Getimians<br /> Abyssals<br /> Liminals<br /> Infernals<br /> ???<br /> Alchemicals<br /> ???<br /> ???</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they'll do Sidereals and Getimians back-to-back, or Abyssals and Liminals really. Actually, maybe Getimians won't even receive a hardback? I think the previous devs said not all the new Exalts will get a big ol' hardcover (though I don't see why not).<br /> <br /> I think after Exigents will come Abyssals. They're new in-universe, iconic dark anti-heroes/villains, and literal opposites of Solars; it'd be good to have them early. I think one of the old devs said Abyssals were initially slated for 2015 back when things were first laid out, which would be pretty early in the game's run if Ex3 was slated for 2013.<br /> <br /> So Abyssals, Sidereals, Liminals, Getimians, Infernals, something new, Alchemicals, and the other new ones following, I think. I'm pretty torn about Lunars and Exigents being swapped, but I want them all out anyway.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T21:53:19-07:00","id":1127919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1127857#post1127857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very good news. As far as I'm concerned, all the new types should be moved to the end of the release schedule. While perhaps more interesting as thought exercises in new types of Exalts, the 3rd Edition additional types can really wait until when/if the older established Exalts become officially playable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't go that far. I mean, let's be honest, Alchemicals are FUN but in terms of how important it is to get them out, they're kind of THE least urgent to get into Creation. We can wait on Alchemicals.<br /> <br /> I'd say that Getimians and Liminals should definitely be out before Alchemicals... Probably even before the Infernals.<br /> <br /> I can't speak for the Blankity-Blanks, the Chosen of the Depths, or the Speakers (I THINK those were teased names do NOT quote me on that) since without knowing a darn thing about them I can't say how important and influential they are in Creation.<br /> <br /> Exigents, however, I can see justification for them being before Abyssals (potentially after), because as mentioned, the Exigent book will also help build up Exalts for people who need them before the book is out.<br /> <br /> On the original topic, I honestly don't mind this. While I utterly adore a few types of Exalts more than Lunars (Sidereals, chiefly) I can see every reason for them to be released after the DBs. Plus, well, to beat the dead horse that had its heart eaten by a Lunar... I'm interested in seeing a thematically cohesive and together theme and a functional charmset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T23:34:43-07:00","id":1127947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1127893#post1127893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they'll do Sidereals and Getimians back-to-back, or Abyssals and Liminals really. Actually, maybe Getimians won't even receive a hardback? I think the previous devs said not all the new Exalts will get a big ol' hardcover (though I don't see why not).<br /> <br /> I think after Exigents will come Abyssals. They're new in-universe, iconic dark anti-heroes/villains, and literal opposites of Solars; it'd be good to have them early. I think one of the old devs said Abyssals were initially slated for 2015 back when things were first laid out, which would be pretty early in the game's run if Ex3 was slated for 2013.<br /> <br /> So Abyssals, Sidereals, Liminals, Getimians, Infernals, something new, Alchemicals, and the other new ones following, I think. I'm pretty torn about Lunars and Exigents being swapped, but I want them all out anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original devs' plan was to have Abyssals and Liminals in the same year. Jumping off that thematic linking, having Sidereals and Getimians as a pair also made sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T00:32:11-07:00","id":1127958,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see. Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T02:04:26-07:00","id":1127978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1127919#post1127919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't speak for the Blankity-Blanks, the Chosen of the Depths, or the Speakers (I THINK those were teased names do NOT quote me on that) since without knowing a darn thing about them I can't say how important and influential they are in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoken. The Niobraran League Exalted were called the Spoken.<br /> <br /> Since they're all deader than disco, though, I don't think we need a splatbook about them... unless the Niobrarans are making a comeback to Creation, that is. Could be an interesting optional subplot, the West would benefit from more stuff happening.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T02:34:05-07:00","id":1127988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1127815#post1127815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope not. Sidereals are more of a setting pillar involved in core conflicts of other major pillar splats. Abyssals (while no less awesome if done right) are a new X factor to the setting (in universe I mean, not that they're new to third edition) far less automatically entwined with the built in conflicts of Lunars, Solars, and Dragon-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also hope to see Sidereals before Abyssals because a)I love Sidereals conceptually, but never played one (partly because of the charmset: both because it was bad mechanically, and because it didn't quite do what I wanted), and b)Abyssals are by far the easiest splat to homebrew, as you just take Solar charms and make them look eeevil.<br /> But I still expect Abyssals before Sidereals, because they tend to come up in games more.<br /> They might also be one the easier splats to write in some ways... not sure if that makes a difference, but it might.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-12-2017, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T04:01:19-07:00","id":1127999,"title":"","content":"I'd rather have Exigents. Much more interesting than the boring Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T04:11:28-07:00","id":1128000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1127978#post1127978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spoken. The Niobraran League Exalted were called the Spoken.<br /> <br /> Since they're all deader than disco, though, I don't think we need a splatbook about them... unless the Niobrarans are making a comeback to Creation, that is. Could be an interesting optional subplot, the West would benefit from more stuff happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both the Spoken and the Chosen of the Depths were Niobraran League Exalted.<br /> <br /> From what the previous devs said, the Niobraran War was not a war of extermination, or at least not a<i> total</i> war of extermination, as they intended Heroes of the Niobraran to enable you to play modern-day members of the races who survived the war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T07:54:37-07:00","id":1128043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans#post1127764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From rpg.net<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, that means it's very possible Lunars could be out in 2018!<br /> <br /> After DB, this is the book my playgroup most wants/needs, so having both of those would go a long way to making Exalted 3rd edition feel like a full game.<br /> <br /> It might even make me want to run Exalted again!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hahaha, YES! Lunars! IMO, at minimum, you need DBs, Solars and Lunars to run a game of Exalted. DBs because they rule the world, will be your antagonists most of the time and have the strongest support structure, Solars because they're the catalyst that will shape the new age, and the Lunars because they're the most visible and immediate of the Anathema threats. (The Solars are still trickling back in, the Abyssals have only just now become a clear threat, the Infernals are still in hell and may or may not exist, the Alchemicals aren't here yet, you get the idea)<br /> <br /> I might be biased, but w/e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T11:14:34-07:00","id":1128097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NullApostle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1127999#post1127999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather have Exigents. Much more interesting than the boring Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>See I think it's mindsets like that that make Vance want to go &quot;Yes but what if Lunars like... WEREN'T dull?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T11:37:00-07:00","id":1128105,"title":"","content":"I honestly would rather Exigents first. I need this homebrew juice. Like, Lunars are cool, but pushing back the exigents seems...off to me. It's like, here's the thing that lets a determined homebrew make <i>any exalted they need in playable form. </i>I was kinda annoyed that Exigents were behind Dragonblooded, because I could <i>homebrew dragonblooded easier with exigents.</i>. Same with Lunars, Infernals, Siderals, or even weird one off stuff. Exigents, as a book, just seem infintely more valuable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T12:58:09-07:00","id":1128131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1127919#post1127919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't go that far. I mean, let's be honest, Alchemicals are FUN but in terms of how important it is to get them out, they're kind of THE least urgent to get into Creation. We can wait on Alchemicals.<br /> <br /> I'd say that Getimians and Liminals should definitely be out before Alchemicals... Probably even before the Infernals.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, my statement was overly broad. To rephrase, I'd prefer new stuff get moved after what I consider &quot;setting vital&quot; Exalted types - DBs, Lunars, Sidereals, and Abyssals. Infernals and Alchemicals happen to be my personal favorites, but I recognize that neither is as vital to the setting as the big 5, so I'm fine with them going last. It feels like the new stuff should be in that same category.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T13:43:39-07:00","id":1128164,"title":"","content":"Hmmmkay. I'd have taken Exigents first, but fine, I get that Lunars are classics. I am curious to see what direction they go in, particularly since they are the least thematically pinned down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T15:59:47-07:00","id":1128234,"title":"","content":"Printing the Lunar Exalted is more important, since it gives the Dragon-Blooded their Usual Suspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T16:24:09-07:00","id":1128244,"title":"","content":"I personally would have probably preferred Exigents first, but the rationale for printing Lunars first makes total sense to me. Plus it'll make several of my usual players extremely happy, which is always a bonus. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T21:58:16-07:00","id":1128334,"title":"","content":"Well I am quite pleased Dragon Blooded and Lunars are must haves I need as soon as possible. I can homebrew Exigents till they arrive, as they are just... canon homebrews. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T06:04:36-07:00","id":1128408,"title":"","content":"That's nice. But I won't dance or anything until I have Arms of the Chosen. It is already late, and I'm worried that will carry on to the hardbacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T06:22:37-07:00","id":1128413,"title":"","content":"They could really push back Infernal to the end because there are only 50 Infernal Exalted. I really wish that they had progressed by population in 3e, though I know that would have been unpopular on this forum. In an ideal world, I would have preferred DB and Lunar before Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T09:37:32-07:00","id":1128491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128413#post1128413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could really push back Infernal to the end because there are only 50 Infernal Exalted. I really wish that they had progressed by population in 3e, though I know that would have been unpopular on this forum. In an ideal world, I would have preferred DB and Lunar before Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it wouldn't have been unpopular just on these forums. DBs before Solars would feel so weird and leave the core protagonists of the game in the cold for so long, I really don't think it would be a viable decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T10:28:39-07:00","id":1128503,"title":"","content":"The story of the Solar Exalted as the returning rightful kings wouldn't ring as true for the player base if they were anything but the first splat of each Edition.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, there would have been great merit in printing the Exalted in descending order of rarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T10:33:20-07:00","id":1128504,"title":"","content":"The Lunars, DBs, and Solars are kind of the most important exalted in the world currently, frankly all three could make a case for initial release rights based on how much they define the setting. <br /> <br /> As much as I want the exigent charm guidelines, if i was determining release order those would be the first three books with arms of the chosen and exigents being on the second priority tier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11837,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","user":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","date":". 08-13-2017, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T11:13:21-07:00","id":1128518,"title":"","content":"I disagree about the Lunar Exalted. They should always be second or third, and never the first. The first should always be the Solars or the Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T12:04:01-07:00","id":1128534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128105#post1128105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly would rather Exigents first. I need this homebrew juice. Like, Lunars are cool, but pushing back the exigents seems...off to me. It's like, here's the thing that lets a determined homebrew make <i>any exalted they need in playable form. </i>I was kinda annoyed that Exigents were behind Dragonblooded, because I could <i>homebrew dragonblooded easier with exigents.</i>. Same with Lunars, Infernals, Siderals, or even weird one off stuff. Exigents, as a book, just seem infintely more valuable.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, a part of the player base doesn't homebrew, or uses homebrew from other people, or cannot use homebrew, but still want to play DB, Lunars, Abyssals. I would guess, that this part of the player base is pretty big, even the majority of players. On the other side, even people, who do use homebrew seldom go all the way to build themself a whole splat from scratch. I know I cannot even bring myself to homebrew my own evocation set. No time, no motivation, no idea. And that is for a set in the range of 4-6 charms. Not 10, not 20 and certainly not 150 and more. And every charm needs some balance, something interesting, some flavor. This is a task, where only a small group of players will be able to achive it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/47-lc1984","name":"LC1984","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar47_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T12:49:04-07:00","id":1128553,"title":"","content":"People severely overstate how easy it'd be to homebrew the big splats using the Exigents book. It's going to have <i>guidelines</i> for creating your own <i>Exigents</i>. unique, or semi-Unique, Exalted bound to a particular god. It's a completely different scale from the Celestials and Dragon-Blooded. It's likely going to be helpful in terms of setting expectations and such, but it's not going to magically make it any less of a huge undertaking. By treating it as a &quot;make anything you want&quot; toolkit, people are setting themselves up for a massive disappointment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","user":"Morty","date":". 08-13-2017, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T13:12:35-07:00","id":1128561,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I agree. Homebrewing your one single character's charm set* based on the guidelines would be much easier than homebrewing an entire charmset suitable for many different character types.<br /> <br /> *Which, quite likely, you wouldn't do all at once: I mean, you don't really need to design the Essence 5 charms when you make the character.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I think Exigents sounds like the hardest book to write, so it's probably good for the writers to have already done more than DBs+a bit of the core by the time they get to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T13:58:13-07:00","id":1128569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128503#post1128503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The story of the Solar Exalted as the returning rightful kings wouldn't ring as true for the player base if they were anything but the first splat of each Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'd say that depends a bit on how that story is framed; more emphasis on the idea that ancient reincarnated kings is something sinister and disruptive, in other words where the primary story is not <i>being</i> those kings, and it would be serviceable to put them later, if at all.<br /> <br /> But that's really the question for a different game with a different tone; perhaps not quite World of Darkness, but showing those roots a bit more.<br /> <br /> Hmm, now I want to check the Making Of book again and see if Grabowski said that the decision to refocus the game on the Solars came before or after the realisation that there would be several practical difficulties with effectively realising the idea of them as the strongest if they weren't also the yardstick.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T15:30:40-07:00","id":1128591,"title":"","content":"I think that if the game started with the Dragon-Blooded, everyone would fully accept the idea that the Dragon-Blooded are the rightful rulers of the world. After all, they successfully killed the last guys and have been ruling the world for the last thousand years or so. Most of humanity doesn't remember a time when the Dragon-Blooded didn't rule.<br /> <br /> If the Solar Exalted were released after the Lunar Exalted, they would FEEL less like kings returning to take back their kingdoms, and more like the old Deathlords -- sore loser ghosts rising from the grave to destroy the world again.<br /> <br /> I think the Solar Exalted being the first gives them a legitimacy in the eyes of most players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T16:40:57-07:00","id":1128613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128553#post1128553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People severely overstate how easy it'd be to homebrew the big splats using the Exigents book. It's going to have <i>guidelines</i> for creating your own <i>Exigents</i>. unique, or semi-Unique, Exalted bound to a particular god. It's a completely different scale from the Celestials and Dragon-Blooded. It's likely going to be helpful in terms of setting expectations and such, but it's not going to magically make it any less of a huge undertaking. By treating it as a &quot;make anything you want&quot; toolkit, people are setting themselves up for a massive disappointment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean, I meant for making my own versions of exalted that are far, far away. If I have a player that wants to play an Infernal/Nocturnal/Whatever, the Exigent book would still be helpful. A guide line like that, that helps me understanding mechanics, deisgn philosphy, scaling, etc would make my life infintely easier, because my alternative is working from scratch. Charm guidlines are going to be useful for either, especially since we've been told some exigents do run all the way up to Solar levels in their area.<br /> <br /> I'm colored also by having only had 2 players intreasted in lunars, and myself not finding them that intreasting compared to other splats (Abyssals are next to them on the 'eh' scale). That and Exigents is the single book I'm most excited for and would have pushed to 'right after solars'. Dragonblooded I got because they are the most common exalted, and I understand from a lore perspective why to include lunars next.<br /> I just was hoping them and sids would wait till after exigents.<br /> Edit:<br /> I'm also an ST that relies heavily on and is rather comfortable using homebrew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T16:56:13-07:00","id":1128617,"title":"","content":"I generally have only run DB games because my players found Celestial Exalted to be boring because they were too powerful. There is something much more satisfying about a DB circle confronting and defeating an Abyssal than a Solar circle doing the same. The former is a triumph, the latter is bullying.<br /> <br /> I do wonder what Exalted would be like if it was presented from the DB/Lunar perspective rather than from the Solar perspective. The Solar Exalted (and by extension the Abyssal and Infernal Exalted) would become primordial threats to the social order. The legitimacy of the Solar Exalted would be questioned because there would be no guarantees that the old abuses would not occur again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T17:07:20-07:00","id":1128622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128591#post1128591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that if the game started with the Dragon-Blooded, everyone would fully accept the idea that the Dragon-Blooded are the rightful rulers of the world. After all, they successfully killed the last guys and have been ruling the world for the last thousand years or so. Most of humanity doesn't remember a time when the Dragon-Blooded didn't rule.<br /> <br /> If the Solar Exalted were released after the Lunar Exalted, they would FEEL less like kings returning to take back their kingdoms, and more like the old Deathlords -- sore loser ghosts rising from the grave to destroy the world again.<br /> <br /> I think the Solar Exalted being the first gives them a legitimacy in the eyes of most players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree with this. Granted, I have more than a few people in my group who would rather they <i>didn't</i> have that legitimacy, but it still is what it is (and I personally prefer Solars being first anyway).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T17:15:13-07:00","id":1128628,"title":"","content":"If the Solar Exalted didn't come first, they honestly wouldn't be sufficiently distinguishable from the Infernals or Abyssals.<br /> <br /> If the Solar Exalted don't have the feel of legitimacy, then the argument of whether or not they can be a good thing for Creation becomes rather one-sided. The game and the world clearly didn't need them at the beginning, so why does it need them now? They're just introducing more chaos that the Dragon-Blooded have to deal with.<br /> <br /> But since the Solar Exalted come first, the game and the world is grounded in the fact that the Solar Exalted built and ruled a BETTER world than what Creation currently is. Well, &quot;better&quot;, in at least some regard. But at least how much better becomes an actual question and two-sided debate, with pros and cons on both sides.<br /> <br /> Creation can never return to the First Age, and probably shouldn't even if it could... but it can never forget or ignore the First Age. It shouldn't be able to forget or ignore the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> That's why the Solar Exalted have to come first. Quite simply, they are the host whose Chosen make the biggest immediate impact on an individual level, and their return to Creation is one of the biggest impacts to the setting in its history. It's the most powerful and dramatic beginning for every Edition before and any Edition to come.<br /> <br /> This is <i>Exalted</i>. It has to start with a bang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T01:13:34-07:00","id":1128729,"title":"","content":"I think you're overstating it. The Dragonborn could have set themselves up into a position where they could make the claim to being the ones keeping creation together, but it's pretty clear they're doing a poor job of it, and the lunar are pretty terrible at it too. <br /> <br /> That said, it does play into the importance of the solaroids, the Lunars and the DBs are in a stalemate. Without the disruption caused by the Solars coming back en masse, there'd really be very little to break the stasis.<br /> <br /> So in that respect the solars really do need to be the initial focus, because without them the story doesn't progress.<br /> <br /> Hmmmmmm.....<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T05:03:18-07:00","id":1128760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128729#post1128729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, it does play into the importance of the solaroids, the Lunars and the DBs are in a stalemate. Without the disruption caused by the Solars coming back en masse, there'd really be very little to break the stasis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmmmnope. In the war of attrition, the Lunars are winning. It's not a <i>quick</i> victory, but every First Age weapon the Dragon-Blooded exhaust against the Lunars is one they can never replenish; likewise, every scion of the Scarlet Dynasty killed in the fighting is gone forever, where casualties among the Lunars will reincarnate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T06:04:15-07:00","id":1128775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128760#post1128760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmmmnope. In the war of attrition, the Lunars are winning. It's not a <i>quick</i> victory, but every First Age weapon the Dragon-Blooded exhaust against the Lunars is one they can never replenish; likewise, every scion of the Scarlet Dynasty killed in the fighting is gone forever, where casualties among the Lunars will reincarnate.</div> </div> </div> </div>The disappearance of the Empress wouldn't have helped matters, either, since that deprives the Empire of its biggest stick: the Sword of Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T06:09:43-07:00","id":1128777,"title":"","content":"The DB can breed much greater numbers (look at Lookshy), but I think that the governing structure of the Realm allowed for the protracted death by a thousand cuts caused by the Lunars. I think that if the Realm was structured in the fashion of Lookshy, with the DB population ratio being 1:100, then I think that the Lunars would be just an annoyance because the Realm would have the capability to maintain a basic First Age military infrastructure (Lookshy has difficulties because it is only a city-state, not because the DB of Lookshy are innately incompetent). As it stands now though, the Lunars are slowly winning because they are producing hundreds of times more Beastmen than there are DBs and because they are capable of replacing their First Age military infrastructure while the DB of the Realm would rather bugger beautiful slave children than dedicate themselves to maintaining their civilization or reduce their individual privileges by expanding their numbers. Of course, if the Solars were facing a Realm that was structured like Lookshy (with one million DB among the one hundred million mortals), they would probably not survive for more than a few months per incarnation before they were caught and executed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T07:40:51-07:00","id":1128809,"title":"","content":"Oh, so that's where the idea for your thread came from. No, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a> , &quot;producing beastmen&quot; isn't why the Lunars are winning (nor, by the way, are they &quot;maintaining First Age military infrastructure&quot; - they're using guerilla tactics precisely because they can't); no, &quot;a Realm structured like Lookshy&quot; would not steamroll the setting (or at least, not any better than the Realm as-is already does); and no, the Realm having a million DBs (which is actually rather different from a Realm structured like Lookshy) would not magically let them resurrect or even maintain long-term the fallen military structures of the First Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-14-2017, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T08:05:29-07:00","id":1128826,"title":"","content":"Something else worth considering is that (unless it's being written out) the DB's blood is thinning: DBs now tend to have weaker breeding, and be less likely to exalt, so over the long run, there'll be less and less DBs, with weaker breeding.*<br /> <br /> *Although this is much less of an issue now lower breeding doesn't mean less motes!<br /> <br /> Of course, that's a very long term thing, but the number of Lunars isn't going to go down. So attrition is on their side.<br /> But that's a very, very, slow process.<br /> <br /> Of course, recently they've got a big boost as the Empress has vanished, as Sunder mentioned, and the Realm is suddenly distracted both by that and by all these Solars as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, good points from Sunder there. I think if they had gone with the original plan of having DBs first and then Solars, while that would have been interesting, it probably would have made Solars less inspiring for players. Solars are the most default of protagonists by their very nature, and so work best as the starting characters. They need least knowledge of the setting, fit pc archetypes most easily, etc.<br /> <br /> Though admittedly I wouldn't mind running a game for players who don't know the Solar background and actually think they are straight-up demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T08:22:43-07:00","id":1128833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128591#post1128591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that if the game started with the Dragon-Blooded, everyone would fully accept the idea that the Dragon-Blooded are the rightful rulers of the world. After all, they successfully killed the last guys and have been ruling the world for the last thousand years or so. Most of humanity doesn't remember a time when the Dragon-Blooded didn't rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI want to think that a lot of modern players are a hard sell on the starting concept of rightful rulers, but considering some threads...<br /> <br /> \u200bRegardless, it still depends on presentation a bit; still referring to the tone of World of Darkness games, I find it to be possible to present a starting group that is riddled with issues even while they're set against the sinister premise of ancient, mysterious, fearsome kings returning to the world after a long absence<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Solar Exalted were released after the Lunar Exalted, they would FEEL less like kings returning to take back their kingdoms, and more like the old Deathlords -- sore loser ghosts rising from the grave to destroy the world again.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can be both.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T08:29:13-07:00","id":1128841,"title":"","content":"Anyway, as for the book orders, there's no right or wrong answer; either configuration benefits somebody (there are people who will benefit more from Lunars coming out concretely first rather than needing to improvise with the aid of Exigents), and if one of a person's reasons for wanting Exigents is to have had help in making many others, there isn't really a consolation that can fill in for that. Sometimes that's just how it goes.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, none of this is ideal; at this point, involvement in Exalted generally requires a bit of reconciliation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T09:33:48-07:00","id":1128856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128833#post1128833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI want to think that a lot of modern players are a hard sell on the starting concept of rightful rulers...\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually the problem my players have with Solars... the ones who take it seriously can't buy into the idea of Solars as returning god-kings.<br /> (Others enjoy it ironically, so it's fine)<br /> <br /> But yeah, Isator is right. Everyone wants certain splats in certain orders, because that's the ones that are useful to them. If that's different for different people, not much you can do about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-14-2017, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T10:16:14-07:00","id":1128865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128833#post1128833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can be both.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if they're first.<br /> <br /> Fairly sure it's easier to show the Solars' bad side after presenting them as heroes than it would be to present them as potential heroes after showing them as Anathema.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T10:22:23-07:00","id":1128867,"title":"","content":"The real reason Exalted begins with the Solars is that the <i>whole point</i> of the game is to play a ridiculously powerful demigod, and while all the Exalted embody that to an extent, the Solars are the most straightforward and pure example. Starting with the most powerful splat is a deliberate thematic choice and affects the tone of the entire setting.<br /> <br /> &quot;Exalted is a game about playing ridiculously powerful god-kings who can change the world! To get you started, here's the weakest kind, who are by default heavily tied to the status quo.&quot; It just doesn't match with how the game is framed or marketed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T11:29:45-07:00","id":1128886,"title":"","content":"Oddly never had the solar problem. Mainly cuz I referred to it as &quot;hero&quot; instead of king, made clear that their past lives weren't always great, and then focused on their personal heroics. And heavily downplayed any notion of rightful ruler as opposed to lost power(except the actual queen who exalted.)<br /> Also of their past lives only half had nations...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T12:01:55-07:00","id":1128900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128569#post1128569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI'd say that depends a bit on how that story is framed; more emphasis on the idea that ancient reincarnated kings is something sinister and disruptive, in other words where the primary story is not <i>being</i> those kings, and it would be serviceable to put them later, if at all.<br /> <br /> But that's really the question for a different game with a different tone; perhaps not quite World of Darkness, but showing those roots a bit more.<br /> <br /> Hmm, now I want to check the Making Of book again and see if Grabowski said that the decision to refocus the game on the Solars came before or after the realisation that there would be several practical difficulties with effectively realising the idea of them as the strongest if they weren't also the yardstick.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may offer my own perspective on why the Solars need to come first (assuming that we can't put more than one Exalt type out immediately): there's a few different reasons.<br /> <br /> 1) Solars need to take a prominent role - The current age of Exalted is defined as one of history's major turning points. The old guard (the Realm) is starting to fade as all empires do, and are leaving a power vaccuum. The major change for this age is caused by not just the Solars but their immediate mirror opposites; the Abyssals. They are the great movers and shakers of this world. The Sidereals, DBs and Lunars are all to varying degrees trying to protect their status quo.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not saying Exalted <b>can't</b> be a game where the DB are the main protagonists or even that it <b>shouldn't</b> (in fact it would actually fit better with east asia's culture given its emphasis on group power) but if you do do that how do you frame the Solars? If they're the big defining moment of the age, where does that leave the PCs? You would need to either remove the Solars and Abyssals (likely by setting the main &quot;timeline&quot; of the game BEFORE they begin to regain prominence). The Solars' return is meant to be a huge deal, something that no one can really ignore. But if you take them out of the game... well then you can just ignore them. :P<br /> <br /> &quot;You could make their return sinister and make them the bad guys&quot;<br /> Then what do you do with the Abyssals? The guys who are literally deathknights? It's hard to frame the Solars as the bad guys while having Literally Their Opposites running around as basically the same bad guy after a trip to Hot Topic. If you have both Solars and Abyssals running around as the bad guys, they quickly become redundant, since their power sets are so similar. It could create a very interesting scenario to have one set of bad guys be there to build things up (Solars) and the other to tear them down (Abyssals), to be sure, but you'd need to get deep into the campaign/setting to see that.<br /> <br /> And that's ignoring that the Anathema's nature is supposed to be a secret :P<br /> <br /> 2) They fit new players better than DBs or Lunars. - This may be a bit of bias on my part, but I feel that when you have an established setting your players' characters should know about what the players themselves do. Whatever you throw new players into should be as undefined as possible, so they have little chance to mess with the setting too much. A Solar's backstory can be basically anything, and the memories they get from their first age incarnation happened so long ago that they might as well be hallucinations. If a Solar wants to be a farmer that's never even heard of the Realm, it's a bit of a stretch, but Creation is so vast you can do that.<br /> <br /> A Dragon-blooded, otoh, is a noble in a vast empire and has been training to be one ever since he/she exalted (around 10-12, iirc). There's only so much you can get away with this character getting wrong or not knowing. Even an outcaste (probably the best option for a new player who wants to go DB) is going to have issues. As such, you shouldn't be giving players DB characters until they're more familiar with the setting and system, or playing with other players who are. Granted, that has its own problems, but I feel throwing newbies into a fully-established imperial court creates bigger ones.<br /> <br /> 3) Solar arcs mirror heroic arcs - Let's think for a second about how a typical solar's journey may go. He lives a normal life until it's not normal, then Exalts. For simplicity's sake let's say he's a Dawn and that we're looking at this story from his perspective. He now has an Evil Empire (again, from his perspective) on his heels wherever he goes, so he needs to maintain a low-ish profile. He's strong enough in a fight that he can handle himself, but not so strong that he can afford to be reckless/careless. He can have wise old mentors in the form of gold-faction Sidereals or Lunars. His presence will shape whatever area he's in to his desires as main characters usually do. His journey will be about making his own way in the world, achieving his desires and potentially even ruling the entire world.<br /> <br /> This is the hero's journey at its most basic, and the Solars present it in a way that's easy to understand.<br /> <br /> A Dragon-blooded, otoh, is a servant of the current status quo. Theirs is a story of noblesse oblige, of imperial majesty and dynasties. They're in the setting to try and restore the Realm to its former glory, and to unite the world under one banner. Also a cool story, but it's a very different sort of conflict, and this game is primarily about being a badass hero (see #4).<br /> <br /> 4) What Aquillion said earlier about them being the strongest and thematics and blah blah blah.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Of course none of that would matter if more than one exalted type were fully statted in the corebook. *twitch* I get that you can't throw 5 essence worth of charms for all characters into a single book but you could do it for E1 or E2 for two or three Exalt types (Solars, DBs and Lunars plz) and entirely avoid these problems!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128856#post1128856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is actually the problem my players have with Solars... the ones who take it seriously can't buy into the idea of Solars as returning god-kings.<br /> (Others enjoy it ironically, so it's fine)<br /> <br /> But yeah, Isator is right. Everyone wants certain splats in certain orders, because that's the ones that are useful to them. If that's different for different people, not much you can do about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Solars have so much power that they can just <b>become</b> a king whenever they want and the players tend to assume that's the end goal anyway, it fits well enough. Sure, nobody today really believes in the concept of a &quot;rightful ruler chosen by heaven&quot; but it's a medieval style setting and the players probably want to be that powerful at some point anyway so why not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T12:35:33-07:00","id":1128914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128856#post1128856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is actually the problem my players have with Solars... the ones who take it seriously can't buy into the idea of Solars as returning god-kings.<br /> (Others enjoy it ironically, so it's fine)</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you further explain this, Wizard? Your players can't buy into the idea of Solars as returning god-kings?... Because they don't start out powerful enough? Because of the Wyld Hunt? Because, idk, DotFA spells out they sucked? And how do the other players you have enjoy it ironically?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T12:38:00-07:00","id":1128916,"title":"","content":"Re world changing Solars set a precedent, to be honest, with book priorities as they actually *were*, the degree to which Solars change the world and the Dragonblooded do *not* change the world became exaggerated to the point of parody through the eventual journey through past editions. <br /> <br /> (Almost enveloping anything in this deadening frame where the Dragonblooded in theory couldn't do anything significant and the Solars must constantly do grand, significant things around some faulty dichotomy of &quot;restoring / being unable to restore the First Age&quot;).<br /> <br /> I wouldn't lay this at the feet of the Solars being the first splat published. However if they did put Dragonblooded first, perhaps they would have engaged more with the idea of presenting them as demi-gods who change the world - introducing new ideas to their society, new magic and technology, changing the structure, establishing Houses and domains, doing things differently. And so on for many other Exalted beyond the Solars.<br /> <br /> (On thread topic - good with Lunars, Eric and Robert! Let's see your vision of being chosen by the moon).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T13:17:57-07:00","id":1128937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128865#post1128865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if they're first.<br /> <br /> Fairly sure it's easier to show the Solars' bad side after presenting them as heroes than it would be to present them as potential heroes after showing them as Anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI wonder how Changeling handled the introduction of the Sidhe.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't feel as though the community ever had very much difficulty integrating the more nuance milieu of the Fair Folk after being introduced to them as world-ending monsters.<br /> <br /> Then there's the whole debacle with Guide to the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhy, do you think that What Fire Has Wrought will be incapable of adding dimensions to a Realm that the core heavily emphasises as a world-choking juggernaut?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128867#post1128867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real reason Exalted begins with the Solars is that the <i>whole point</i> of the game is to play a ridiculously powerful demigod</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI feel as though Grabowski's perspective on why he did things is fairly authoritative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128916#post1128916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't lay this at the feet of the Solars being the first splat published. However if they did put Dragonblooded first, perhaps they would have engaged more with the idea of presenting them as demi-gods who change the world - introducing new ideas to their society, new magic and technology, changing the structure, establishing Houses and domains, doing things differently. And so on for many other Exalted beyond the Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bJeez, I'd hardly present the Solars as doing half of these things.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's a very modern perspective that charges changing the world primarily to technological advances, I think.<br /> <br /> \u200bNotwithstanding how the phrase is a bit of a dog-and-pony show.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T13:40:36-07:00","id":1128948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128937#post1128937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a very modern perspective that charges changing the world primarily to technological advances, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that was about 1 in 6 of the ways to change the world I mentioned there (which I will say explicitly were non-exhaustive, if it was not implicit!).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128937#post1128937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though Grabowski's perspective on why he did things is fairly authoritative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though I did not reply to this earlier (as I felt my response possibly a bit mean!), as I'm quoting you now on this, it may be authoritative but not actually that satisfying if you consider the large array of successful games which exist in which designers tend to design the end game (and most powerful characters) *after* the baseline. In that context, it doesn't seem that plausible that designing the Solars last is necessarily an inherent technical difficulty (nor, I guess, to be a bit more arguably mean, does First Edition's execution suggest that designing them first actually helped matters along too much).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":929,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","user":"Ghosthead","date":". 08-14-2017, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T14:26:08-07:00","id":1128961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128948#post1128948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that was about 1 in 6 of the ways to change the world I mentioned there (which I will say explicitly were non-exhaustive, if it was not implicit!).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeeaahh... I feel as though I should withdraw that point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though I did not reply to this earlier (as I felt my response possibly a bit mean!), as I'm quoting you now on this, it may be authoritative but not actually that satisfying if you consider the large array of successful games which exist in which designers tend to design the end game (and most powerful characters) *after* the baseline. In that context, it doesn't seem that plausible that designing the Solars last is necessarily an inherent technical difficulty (nor, I guess, to be a bit more arguably mean, does First Edition's execution suggest that designing them first actually helped matters along too much). </div> </div> </div>I am sincerely interested in exploring this. Could you provide examples?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T15:32:38-07:00","id":1128986,"title":"","content":"Guy