":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T15:35:17-07:00","id":1128989,"title":"","content":"I'm very excited to hear about more Lunar Dominions in Third Edition. I'm sure describing a bunch of those in their book will help really fire the imagination for all the ways that the Lunar Exalted interact with Creation.<br /> <br /> In particular, I'd love to hear what's going on with Raksi in Third Edition, and about His Divine Lunar Presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T15:40:34-07:00","id":1128992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128989#post1128989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm very excited to hear about more Lunar Dominions in Third Edition. I'm sure describing a bunch of those in their book will help really fire the imagination for all the ways that the Lunar Exalted interact with Creation.<br /> <br /> In particular, I'd love to hear what's going on with Raksi in Third Edition, and about His Divine Lunar Presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>His Divine Lunar presence fasinates me because the Caul is...kinda a runaway success the way a lot of places aren't for lunars it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T15:52:07-07:00","id":1128996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128914#post1128914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you further explain this, Wizard? Your players can't buy into the idea of Solars as returning god-kings?... Because they don't start out powerful enough? Because of the Wyld Hunt? Because, idk, DotFA spells out they sucked? And how do the other players you have enjoy it ironically?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I want to answer this, as a Lunar thread, but I guess I should... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I meant they can't buy into the idea of Solars as returning god-kings because they think it's stupid. A)Who cares? What gives Solars the right to be kings, more than anyone else? It's not like Solar PCs are any wiser than any other PCs (I would say, overall, Lunar PCs are very slightly wiser than Solar PCs). And B)what makes Solars think they should be kings? It's not like someone (generally) comes and tells them all &quot;You were made kings of Creation by the Unconquered Sun!&quot;<br /> (Okay, admittedly the first Solar I played did tell the other PCs that... but in retrospect, there wasn't really any reason he should have known that.)<br /> And C)what about all the Solars who know nothing about ruling? Actually, I play a game where the Night Caste is a governor and prince. He's a master of stealth, wrestling, athletics and medicine... and has no idea how to run a city let alone a province. He mostly leaves it to his bureaucrats, and his underlings try and avoid letting him make any decisions because they know his decisions will be incredibly naive.<br /> Supernal Athletics and a ton of Stealth charms do not make you as good at running a province as a mortal bureaucrat, to be frank.<br /> <br /> Actually, the player who most hates Solars (and never plays them) is the one who considers being returning god-kings the most important part of Solars. The players who don't consider being returning god-kings to be an important theme of being a Solar like them much more.<br /> <br /> I mean, don't get me wrong, some Solar PCs do want to rule, but they don't consider it their right because they're Solars. For example, in my recent game, two Solar PCs gained political power. Princess (later Queen) Enhenduanna created a magical mountain kingdom and conquered surrounding regions through diplomacy or dragon-based invasion, and her justification was... she could. And also she was a Princess, so raised to believe she should rule. But none of that was because she was a Solar.<br /> Fulgens Cruciatus manouvred to become supreme war-leader of the Djala, and overthrew some local Djala tribal kings and replaced them with puppets, because he'd been appointed by his god to protect the Djala, and considered this to be the best way to protect them... and also, some Djala wouldn't admit his god was god of all Djala, so he had to beat them up until they did.<br /> <br /> So, extremely able, powerful people may well rise to power, but I haven't really seen (unironic) characters fight to be ruler and genuinely believe &quot;I'm a Solar so I should be in charge.&quot; It's not like becoming a Solar comes with a golden plaque saying &quot;The Unconquered Sun, King of the Gods, says you should be King of Creation.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, I've seen plenty of DBs who think they should rule because they're DBs, but then, they've been raised their whole lives in a religion that preaches that.<br /> <br /> Although, as I said, I have seen people talk about the Solars' right to rule, but it's not something the player's invested in, it's something they consider... ironic? Like the way we play DBs and say &quot;stupid savages, why are they complaing about being ruled by their moral betters, the Dragonblood? Now where are my hookers and blow.&quot; Similarly, Solars saying &quot;everyone should obey us Solars, because we're so morally righteous and sent by the Gods, and we'll kill anyone who disagrees.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> But... I'm not really seeing how this applies to Lunars?<br /> I guess the thing about Lunars is that they don't actually (unlike some other splats) have any ideological belief in their own right to rule. I mean, they may take over societies because they need them to fight the Realm, they may take over societies out of greed or a sense of public duty, and they may take over societies so DBs can't, because f*ck those guys. But young Lunars are not told &quot;as a Lunar, it's your right and duty to rule over mortals&quot; the way DBs are (and some people seem to think Solars are).<br /> Which is perhaps why my players who dislike the returning god-king thing generally like Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-14-2017, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T15:55:31-07:00","id":1128998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128987#post1128987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meerkat's Spotlight Stolen Reversal!</div> </div> </div> </div>Bloody Eclipses, now they're even stealing Lunar charms!<br /> <br /> But soon the Lunars will have a new, unstealable charmset! Not a single charm will have the Eclipse keyword! That'll teach them! And then the Lunars will eat their hearts and steal their faces... that'll <i>really</i> teach them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> His Divine Lunar presence fasinates me because the Caul is...kinda a runaway success the way a lot of places aren't for lunars it seems. </div> </div> </div>It's probably important to have some examples of where the Lunars are just totally kicking ass. They have very much lacked that in the past.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit sceptical about this Black Lion though. He sounds a bit too much like some straight-up awesome leader of the Lunars, and that's not how Lunars roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T16:00:36-07:00","id":1129000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128998#post1128998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's probably important to have some examples of where the Lunars are just totally kicking ass. They have very much lacked that in the past.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit sceptical about this Black Lion though. He sounds a bit too much like some straight-up awesome leader of the Lunars, and that's not how Lunars roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>THATS WHAT FASICN--in door voice, lower excitement. Ahem.<br /> Thats what fascinates me most about him though. He's a lunar in a different landscape, who doesn't feel not lunar(to me). Notable to me is the 3 times reported dead. That reads like a trickster/cunning/folk hero general/warleader more than a glorious conquering one.<br /> I find splats more fasicnating when they can flex into roles not apparently obvious to them, and Sha is doing just that! The caul is almost a lunar run, functional kingdom from my reading! It's a nice takeaway for someone who wants to see Lunar emperors, pharaohs, kings and so on! Because it doesn't quuuuuuite fit the norm for Lunars. It'd be like Dragonblooded rebels/'barbarians' or Sidereal divine crime bosses, or ...okay, thats all I got of the top of my head but yeah!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T16:31:12-07:00","id":1129012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128992#post1128992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> His Divine Lunar presence fasinates me because the Caul is...kinda a runaway success the way a lot of places aren't for lunars it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bFrom the write-up in the Caul, I get the distinct impression that control of the Caul has gone back and forth over the years.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt raises a question; if you repeatedly succeed at convincing people that you're dead, often for centuries at a time, does that not imply that you still failed in some manner? Like &quot;oh, you thought that when I was apparently struck down, my armies were then scattered and destroyed, and control over the island was secured for three generations, that I had been defeated, but I pulled the wool over your eyes!&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Maybe</i> there are frequently scenarios in which pretending to be dead is done for the sake of being able to enact some keikaku out of sight rather than occasionally needing to pretend to be dead to redirect the force that would make you actually dead, but I have some doubts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">He sounds a bit too much like some straight-up awesome leader of the Lunars, and that's not how Lunars roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>It read to me more like an impressive Lunar doing his own thing who occasionally fires the passions of younger Lunars who want to go off and join in. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to hear what's going on with Raksi in Third Edition</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI hold out hope that she shall complete the trifecta of elder Lunars who aren't really involved in the Silver Pact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T16:41:16-07:00","id":1129016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the write-up in the Caul, I get the distinct impression that control of the Caul has gone back and forth over the years.</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression is that the Lunars always had control of parts of the jungle, DBs always had that city, and control of the temples (and probably surrounding settlements, as big temples tend to have surrounding settlements, plus probably roads) went back and forth.<br /> So, basically what you said, I guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1129012#post1129012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It read to me more like an impressive Lunar doing his own thing who occasionally fires the passions of younger Lunars who want to go off and join in.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be fine. Difficult to know at this point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a nice takeaway for someone who wants to see Lunar emperors, pharaohs, kings and so on!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I've got no problem with that. I like seeing those, and sometimes use them in my own games (especially for PCs past lives). In 2nd ed, I felt like they were very obviously missing. In my most recent game, I had a Lunar king/sorcerer whose allies the PCs fought. He wasn't a member of the Silver Pact or anything: he was just a Lunar sorcerer who ruled a city-state as god-king.<br /> <br /> What I meant, is that &quot;His Divine Lunar Presence&quot; sounded to me a bit like a ruler <i>of </i>Lunars.<br /> Maybe he's just ruler/priest of the Lunar-controlled human tribes in the Caul something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI hold out hope that she shall complete the trifecta of elder Lunars who aren't really involved in the Silver Pact.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be good. I'd like to see examples of elders who are not really involved with the Silver Pact, and Raksi seems like a very obvious candidate for that.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Also, thanks guys for bringing the topic back to awesome Lunars and away from those lame new inexperienced Exalts who have hardly any XP or backing or supernatural allies compared to Lunars, and so are much less important than awesome Lunars.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-14-2017, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T17:24:16-07:00","id":1129039,"title":"","content":"I think it would be interesting for a group of Lunar Exalted to create a culture that focused on developing enlightened Terrestrial Exalted who fit the barbarian ideal. Imagine a barbarian nation with a population ratio of 100:1 of mortals to DB? With the support of a few Lunar Exalted, I imagine it could shake the foundations of Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T17:36:57-07:00","id":1129044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1129000#post1129000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reads like a trickster/cunning/folk hero general/warleader more than a glorious conquering one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything about the Black Lion makes me think that he is the perfect guerrilla leader. Lunars have certain obvious advantages when it comes to staying hidden and finding opportunities to strike unexpectedly, and the Black Lion strikes me as the iconic example of Lunars doing the whole &quot;War Against the Realm, War Against Heaven&quot; thing correctly. It's not the norm, but I think that's the point- broadening the norm.<br /> <br /> I'm also tempted, at least in some of my games, to make the Black Lion actually dead, at least this time, and make an adventure out of becoming/finding/grooming his replacement, with special interest in whether or not the PCs try to deceive the opposition into thinking that it's still the Black Lion they face. That way, they maintain the power of his enemies' fear, and turn him into an enemy that's truly impossible to find and kill - a meme of a phantom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T18:04:02-07:00","id":1129055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1129012#post1129012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI hold out hope that she shall complete the trifecta of elder Lunars who aren't really involved in the Silver Pact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I don't have super strong feelings about her association, since I'm open to a good writeup whichever way it goes, what most interests me was the discussion way back of Raksi being more active in pursuing her agenda, whatever that agenda turns out to be. I could see how that could put her in a position where she cooperates with the Silver Pact to try to get them to satisfy her personal quest, or a situation not unlike ma-ha-suchi's, where she sometimes deigns to aid them or avoids them altogether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T18:10:39-07:00","id":1129059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1129044#post1129044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also tempted, at least in some of my games, to make the Black Lion actually dead, at least this time, and make an adventure out of becoming/finding/grooming his replacement, with special interest in whether or not the PCs try to deceive the opposition into thinking that it's still the Black Lion they face. That way, they maintain the power of his enemies' fear, and turn him into an enemy that's truly impossible to find and kill - a meme of a phantom.</div> </div> </div> </div>The secret reveal is that the current Black Lion successor is actually revealed to be the fourth Black Lion. The memetic legacy status of the Black Lion has been going longer than the PCs realize, because There Must Always Be A Black Lion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T18:35:37-07:00","id":1129070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128996#post1128996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure I want to answer this, as a Lunar thread, but I guess I should... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I meant they can't buy into the idea of Solars as returning god-kings because they think it's stupid. A)Who cares? What gives Solars the right to be kings, more than anyone else? It's not like Solar PCs are any wiser than any other PCs (I would say, overall, Lunar PCs are very slightly wiser than Solar PCs). And B)what makes Solars think they should be kings? It's not like someone (generally) comes and tells them all &quot;You were made kings of Creation by the Unconquered Sun!&quot;<br /> (Okay, admittedly the first Solar I played did tell the other PCs that... but in retrospect, there wasn't really any reason he should have known that.)<br /> And C)what about all the Solars who know nothing about ruling? Actually, I play a game where the Night Caste is a governor and prince. He's a master of stealth, wrestling, athletics and medicine... and has no idea how to run a city let alone a province. He mostly leaves it to his bureaucrats, and his underlings try and avoid letting him make any decisions because they know his decisions will be incredibly naive.<br /> Supernal Athletics and a ton of Stealth charms do not make you as good at running a province as a mortal bureaucrat, to be frank.<br /> <br /> Actually, the player who most hates Solars (and never plays them) is the one who considers being returning god-kings the most important part of Solars. The players who don't consider being returning god-kings to be an important theme of being a Solar like them much more.<br /> <br /> I mean, don't get me wrong, some Solar PCs do want to rule, but they don't consider it their right because they're Solars. For example, in my recent game, two Solar PCs gained political power. Princess (later Queen) Enhenduanna created a magical mountain kingdom and conquered surrounding regions through diplomacy or dragon-based invasion, and her justification was... she could. And also she was a Princess, so raised to believe she should rule. But none of that was because she was a Solar.<br /> Fulgens Cruciatus manouvred to become supreme war-leader of the Djala, and overthrew some local Djala tribal kings and replaced them with puppets, because he'd been appointed by his god to protect the Djala, and considered this to be the best way to protect them... and also, some Djala wouldn't admit his god was god of all Djala, so he had to beat them up until they did.<br /> <br /> So, extremely able, powerful people may well rise to power, but I haven't really seen (unironic) characters fight to be ruler and genuinely believe &quot;I'm a Solar so I should be in charge.&quot; It's not like becoming a Solar comes with a golden plaque saying &quot;The Unconquered Sun, King of the Gods, says you should be King of Creation.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, I've seen plenty of DBs who think they should rule because they're DBs, but then, they've been raised their whole lives in a religion that preaches that.<br /> <br /> Although, as I said, I have seen people talk about the Solars' right to rule, but it's not something the player's invested in, it's something they consider... ironic? Like the way we play DBs and say &quot;stupid savages, why are they complaing about being ruled by their moral betters, the Dragonblood? Now where are my hookers and blow.&quot; Similarly, Solars saying &quot;everyone should obey us Solars, because we're so morally righteous and sent by the Gods, and we'll kill anyone who disagrees.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> But... I'm not really seeing how this applies to Lunars?<br /> I guess the thing about Lunars is that they don't actually (unlike some other splats) have any ideological belief in their own right to rule. I mean, they may take over societies because they need them to fight the Realm, they may take over societies out of greed or a sense of public duty, and they may take over societies so DBs can't, because f*ck those guys. But young Lunars are not told &quot;as a Lunar, it's your right and duty to rule over mortals&quot; the way DBs are (and some people seem to think Solars are).<br /> Which is perhaps why my players who dislike the returning god-king thing generally like Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solars get to be god-kings because they're going to take leadership roles one way or another. That's basically it, and it's not a very good justification. Heck, my current dawn is actually high priestess to Zelos, god of strength. She's <b>subordinate</b> to him (kinda - she's not really very good at her job)<br /> <br /> I'd argue that the Solars lost their &quot;right to rule by divine mandate&quot; when Sol turned his face away from them, if anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128989#post1128989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm very excited to hear about more Lunar Dominions in Third Edition. I'm sure describing a bunch of those in their book will help really fire the imagination for all the ways that the Lunar Exalted interact with Creation.<br /> <br /> In particular, I'd love to hear what's going on with Raksi in Third Edition, and about His Divine Lunar Presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it have to be land?<br /> <br /> &quot;I hereby claim every third-born daughter in this city as part of my dominion! COME TO ME, MY LOVELIES!! .... wait, who are all of you men and why do you have torches and pitchfoOHGODDESSI'MONFIRE!!!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T18:36:07-07:00","id":1129071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1129059#post1129059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The secret reveal is that the current Black Lion successor is actually revealed to be the fourth Black Lion. The memetic legacy status of the Black Lion has been going longer than the PCs realize, because There Must Always Be A Black Lion</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's it precisely. On one hand, I like the idea that the Black Lion is tricky enough to fake his own death, only for the surprise reveal later on to just wreck the enemy's morale, but the rumored deaths just seem to invite the &quot;secretly actually dead&quot; twist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T18:48:29-07:00","id":1129075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1129055#post1129055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. I don't have super strong feelings about her association, since I'm open to a good writeup whichever way it goes, what most interests me was the discussion way back of Raksi being more active in pursuing her agenda, whatever that agenda turns out to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI am personally enamoured of my own image, in which Raksi is largely focused on various kinds of sorcerous research, not for the sake of developing things towards practical applications, but to satisfy her own curiosities; that she's intellectual in a manner where learning things is its own reward. I would see that as something that would play out certain aspects of lines about No Moons to the effect of teasing power out of the meaning of things or dredging terrifying miracles from the hidden corners of the world, to keep her specifically Lunar (even apart from how lines around Twilight Castes tend to specifically reference cloistered academics as something that they are not). Basically, Raksi is a very smart and curious person bestowed with immense power, who leverages it to satisfy that hunger.<br /> <br /> \u200bWell, not developing sorcery for the sake of some application, but still consequently being a quite powerful sorcerer that can <i>be</i> applied to tasks like being able to remain in her city undisturbed. <br /> <br /> \u200bAnd also largely detached from moral considerations. Not as an idea of &quot;Raksi delved too deep, and it drove her mad&quot; or anything, just happening to be a personality with basically no moral centre engaged in a field where the lack of such has many avenues for causing a lot of harm to people. Not to mention how it interacts with a sense that the popular conception of Lunars is an image that would be very convenient to being left alone.<br /> <br /> \u200bDoes anybody else remember that crappy spinoff of the Don Bluth Anastasia movie, where the albino bat is relocated to some kind of fantastical version of Tsarist Russia? The way it portrayed the Baba Yaga as a reclusive old woman (with magic) who cultivates stories about eating children to protect her solitude, that's a step short of how Raksi would work in my conception.<br /> <br /> \u200bHer involvement with members of the Silver Pact and engagement of plans thinking in terms of centuries would ultimately come down in terms of making arrangements intended to prevent anything that could threaten her person or distract her from her work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T21:09:55-07:00","id":1129101,"title":"","content":"Lunar Exalted are probably the most gifted sorcerers in Creation (First Age Lunar Exalted are the most gifted sorcerers in Creation). With their large dice pools (above 20 dice with the appropriate stunts), they are capable of doing Ambition 3 Solar Workings without that much difficulty. In effect, they can remake Creation in ways that the DB cannot even imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T02:16:00-07:00","id":1129151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar Exalted are probably the most gifted sorcerers in Creation (First Age Lunar Exalted are the most gifted sorcerers in Creation). With their large dice pools (above 20 dice with the appropriate stunts), they are capable of doing Ambition 3 Solar Workings without that much difficulty. In effect, they can remake Creation in ways that the DB cannot even imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Sidereals might match them, but there's probably 3-4 times as many Lunar celestial sorcerers as Sidereal celestial sorcerers. And Lunars are more likely to be able to spend a year creating a solar-level ritual than Sidereals. So yeah.<br /> (Thanks for reminding people that in practice it's Lunars who are the most powerful sorcerers in the setting, not Solars. People forget that a lot.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think it would be interesting for a group of Lunar Exalted to create a culture that focused on developing enlightened Terrestrial Exalted who fit the barbarian ideal. Imagine a barbarian nation with a population ratio of 100:1 of mortals to DB? With the support of a few Lunar Exalted, I imagine it could shake the foundations of Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Changing Moon in the game I play originally had the plan of spreading DB exaltation to everyone in Creation. That was her Thousand Streams River project.<br /> She seems to have given up now though, she had a Lunar/Solar half-caste baby and then I think decided that even with a 3-month gestation program, she didn't really want tons of kids. Bad for your figure.<br /> Honestly, breeding programs are really awkward both morally and practically.<br /> Not to say you couldn't create a kingdom with a small number of DB barbarians. But 100:1... well, with monomaniacal focus and strict breeding laws, you might be able to do it over an extremely long time, but it's very much a long-term plan.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also tempted, at least in some of my games, to make the Black Lion actually dead, at least this time, and make an adventure out of becoming/finding/grooming his replacement, with special interest in whether or not the PCs try to deceive the opposition into thinking that it's still the Black Lion they face. That way, they maintain the power of his enemies' fear, and turn him into an enemy that's truly impossible to find and kill - a meme of a phantom.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good plot idea, I like it.<br /> But of course, they're Lunars... maybe all of them can be the Black Lion! Giving him the power to be in multiple places at the same time.<br /> With the 2nd ed charmset, it wasn't that difficult for several PCs to swap being the same character: the Lunars in our game took turns being the Emperor. That way if anyone was suspected of having eaten the Emperor, they could turn up in the same room as the Emperor, proving he was still alive (which obviously he wasn't).<br /> Don't know if that'll still be possible in 3rd ed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. I don't have super strong feelings about her association, since I'm open to a good writeup whichever way it goes, what most interests me was the discussion way back of Raksi being more active in pursuing her agenda, whatever that agenda turns out to be.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bI am personally enamoured of my own image, in which Raksi is largely focused on various kinds of sorcerous research, not for the sake of developing things towards practical applications, but to satisfy her own curiosities; that she's intellectual in a manner where learning things is its own reward. I would see that as something that would play out certain aspects of lines about No Moons to the effect of teasing power out of the meaning of things or dredging terrifying miracles from the hidden corners of the world, to keep her specifically Lunar (even apart from how lines around Twilight Castes tend to specifically reference cloistered academics as something that they are not). Basically, Raksi is a very smart and curious person bestowed with immense power, who leverages it to satisfy that hunger.<br /> <br /> \u200bWell, not developing sorcery for the sake of some application, but still consequently being a quite powerful sorcerer that can <i>be</i> applied to tasks like being able to remain in her city undisturbed.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd also largely detached from moral considerations. Not as an idea of &quot;Raksi delved too deep, and it drove her mad&quot; or anything, just happening to be a personality with basically no moral centre engaged in a field where the lack of such has many avenues for causing a lot of harm to people. Not to mention how it interacts with a sense that the popular conception of Lunars is an image that would be very convenient to being left alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty similar to how I see her (though maybe still a bit mad, just from having lived so long as a Lunar; but her fundamental issue is that she's amoral, not that she's mad).<br /> <br /> Which, I think, can be leveraged into &quot;being more active&quot; fairly easily: not just doing research in her city, but sending out her minions to find stuff she needs for her research. Barbarians might attack a scavenger lord's camp to get the ancient book he just dug up as she thinks it might have useful info; young Lunars might kill a fair folk behemoth because Raksi needs it heart for her sorcerous research, etc.<br /> I think it'd work well for the kind of plot where the protagonist finds, accidentally, some ancient knowledge and the bad guys are coming after him/her because they want the secret.<br /> <br /> Because in previous editions, she didn't really get used much; she was just kind of the boss protecting spellbook loot, but there wasn't much reason to interact with her unless you actually want there, unless you actually tried to write it in specifically (we used her a little because one Lunar PCs backstory was that he used to be one of her apprentices).<br /> And if you don't really interact much with NPCs, there's not much point the writers saying much about them.<br /> <br /> (Which, perhaps, they will not: they may choose to focus on new Lunar NPCs as examples of elders. Which is somewhat reasonable, as the number of written-up Lunar elders isn't that high considering how many Lunars there are and how powerful they are.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Solars get to be god-kings because they're going to take leadership roles one way or another.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's really true. At least, no more than for Lunars.<br /> In the game I recently finished running (got to about 370xp):<br /> <br /> The Eclipse ruled a kingdom<br /> The ghost became a god<br /> The Dawn, Changing Moon and Full Moon were all powerful advisors/council members of the ghost/god's kingdom (essentially, they mostly controlled it between them as the ghost/god ascended<br /> The Twilight, other Eclipse and Zenith did not have leadership positions (and the Twilight was the longest-lived character in this 6 or 7 year game).<br /> <br /> In the game I play:<br /> The Night is a governor/married to the Pharoah's daughter (and is absolutely terrible at ruling)<br /> The Changing Moon is his chief consort<br /> The Fair Folk is her maid<br /> The Eclipse and Zenith are just members of the Night's retinue (well, actually, the Eclipse has just gone on the run because he was accused of murder).<br /> The casteless Lunar was the Night's chief advisor, but he had to go and get tattooed.<br /> And now there's a Twilight just re-joined us after a long hiatus, he's just another member of the Night's retinue (he's an airship captain and engineer... why would he want to be in charge of anything?).<br /> <br /> If characters are not interested in ruling, or good at it, why would they end up in a leadership position? The Twilight in the game I ran was a master of craft and larceny; why should that make him better at ruling than the Changing Moon? Of course, it didn't, which is why the Changing Moon was the party's leader (though she claimed the Twilight was the party's leader, and the Full Moon claimed he was the leader), and the main power behind the throne of the kingdom the ghost PC became ruler of.<br /> Sure, some characters end up in charge because they want to be/are good at it, but it's not inevitable for Solars. If your character is the best swordsmith in Creation, or the best horseman in Creation... well, it's pretty likely they might end up with some servants/assistants/apprentices, but I see them as far less likely to end up in charge of something as a Changing Moon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T03:26:33-07:00","id":1129164,"title":"","content":"What's the qualification for &quot;most powerful sorcerer&quot; here?<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, what kind of numbers are being assumed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T04:57:23-07:00","id":1129183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1128996#post1128996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure I want to answer this, as a Lunar thread, but I guess I should... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I meant they can't buy into the idea of Solars as returning god-kings because they think it's stupid. A)Who cares? What gives Solars the right to be kings, more than anyone else? It's not like Solar PCs are any wiser than any other PCs (I would say, overall, Lunar PCs are very slightly wiser than Solar PCs). And B)what makes Solars think they should be kings? It's not like someone (generally) comes and tells them all &quot;You were made kings of Creation by the Unconquered Sun!&quot;<br /> (Okay, admittedly the first Solar I played did tell the other PCs that... but in retrospect, there wasn't really any reason he should have known that.)<br /> And C)what about all the Solars who know nothing about ruling? Actually, I play a game where the Night Caste is a governor and prince. He's a master of stealth, wrestling, athletics and medicine... and has no idea how to run a city let alone a province. He mostly leaves it to his bureaucrats, and his underlings try and avoid letting him make any decisions because they know his decisions will be incredibly naive.<br /> Supernal Athletics and a ton of Stealth charms do not make you as good at running a province as a mortal bureaucrat, to be frank.<br /> <br /> Actually, the player who most hates Solars (and never plays them) is the one who considers being returning god-kings the most important part of Solars. The players who don't consider being returning god-kings to be an important theme of being a Solar like them much more.<br /> <br /> I mean, don't get me wrong, some Solar PCs do want to rule, but they don't consider it their right because they're Solars. For example, in my recent game, two Solar PCs gained political power. Princess (later Queen) Enhenduanna created a magical mountain kingdom and conquered surrounding regions through diplomacy or dragon-based invasion, and her justification was... she could. And also she was a Princess, so raised to believe she should rule. But none of that was because she was a Solar.<br /> Fulgens Cruciatus manouvred to become supreme war-leader of the Djala, and overthrew some local Djala tribal kings and replaced them with puppets, because he'd been appointed by his god to protect the Djala, and considered this to be the best way to protect them... and also, some Djala wouldn't admit his god was god of all Djala, so he had to beat them up until they did.<br /> <br /> So, extremely able, powerful people may well rise to power, but I haven't really seen (unironic) characters fight to be ruler and genuinely believe &quot;I'm a Solar so I should be in charge.&quot; It's not like becoming a Solar comes with a golden plaque saying &quot;The Unconquered Sun, King of the Gods, says you should be King of Creation.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, I've seen plenty of DBs who think they should rule because they're DBs, but then, they've been raised their whole lives in a religion that preaches that.<br /> <br /> Although, as I said, I have seen people talk about the Solars' right to rule, but it's not something the player's invested in, it's something they consider... ironic? Like the way we play DBs and say &quot;stupid savages, why are they complaing about being ruled by their moral betters, the Dragonblood? Now where are my hookers and blow.&quot; Similarly, Solars saying &quot;everyone should obey us Solars, because we're so morally righteous and sent by the Gods, and we'll kill anyone who disagrees.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> But... I'm not really seeing how this applies to Lunars?<br /> I guess the thing about Lunars is that they don't actually (unlike some other splats) have any ideological belief in their own right to rule. I mean, they may take over societies because they need them to fight the Realm, they may take over societies out of greed or a sense of public duty, and they may take over societies so DBs can't, because f*ck those guys. But young Lunars are not told &quot;as a Lunar, it's your right and duty to rule over mortals&quot; the way DBs are (and some people seem to think Solars are).<br /> Which is perhaps why my players who dislike the returning god-king thing generally like Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I understand now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T05:09:04-07:00","id":1129185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1129164#post1129164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the qualification for &quot;most powerful sorcerer&quot; here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Having lots of different spells at high circles, and being better at casting them (which, mechanically, is represented by bigger dice pools), I guess. I can't see how else you could represent it. I suppose also maybe having more workings already done? Like maybe if one terrestrial sorceress who knows 7 spells lives in a magical mansion full of magical servants she created, I guess you could argue she's more powerful than another sorceress who knows 10 spells.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, how &quot;powerful&quot; a sorcerer is, is going to be a rather vague descriptor, but not one I think is completely meaningless. A mortal sorcerer might know a spell that Raksi doesn't, and so be better at her at that very particular thing, but it's still reasonable to say &quot;Raksi is one of the most poweful sorcerers in Creation&quot;, because she knows lots of terrestrial and celestial spells (and can cast them very well, with a low chance of them failing to do whatever the spell does).<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, what kind of numbers are being assumed? </div> </div> </div>Of sorcerers, do you mean? Or sorcerers of a particular circle?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T05:10:32-07:00","id":1129187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1129101#post1129101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar Exalted are probably the most gifted sorcerers in Creation (First Age Lunar Exalted are the most gifted sorcerers in Creation). With their large dice pools (above 20 dice with the appropriate stunts), they are capable of doing Ambition 3 Solar Workings without that much difficulty. In effect, they can remake Creation in ways that the DB cannot even imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I thought Solars, regardless of what Age we're talking about, were by canon the most powerful sorcerers of Creation. For one, they can cast spells from the Adamant Circle... Lunars can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T05:35:59-07:00","id":1129190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1129185#post1129185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b<br /> Of sorcerers, do you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>How many Lunars would one assume are sorcerers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T06:10:01-07:00","id":1129199,"title":"","content":"It's a good question, but not one I'm sure needs to be given exact numbers. I'd guess about the same proportion as for most other splats, but maybe a bit more than Dragonblood (as there's a certain stigma in the Realm against being a sorcerer), a bit more than Solars (as it's easier for them to get a teacher) and a bit less than Sidereals (that's why I said there's probably 3-4 times as many Lunar sorcerers than Sidereals: there's 4 times as many Lunars, but there may not be 4 times as many Lunar sorcerers).<br /> Of course, for Celestial Sorcerers (which was what I was referring to when talking about power: I'm sure that Mnemon is more powerful than a Lunar who's just learned his first celestial spell, but obviously the most powerful sorcerers in Creation are going to be at least Celestial), the proportion is much lower, but again, I'd guess a bit less than Sidereals.<br /> I'd accept that it could potentially be much lower than the proportion of Sidereal celestial sorcerers, but I reckon it probably would just a bit lower. So overall, you'd have significantly more Lunar celestial sorcerers, just because there are 4-5 times as many Lunars as Sidereals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-15-2017, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T06:20:22-07:00","id":1129200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1129187#post1129187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, I thought Solars, regardless of what Age we're talking about, were by canon the most powerful sorcerers of Creation. For one, they can cast spells from the Adamant Circle... Lunars can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point, is that in 768 RY probably not a single Exalt can cast spells from the Adamant Circle. Maybe, <i>maybe</i>, Samea. I think she's sometimes been depicted in the fluff as being able to. But I think generally, it's probably better for the setting that she's a Celestial sorcerer, which I think is how she's generally been shown.<br /> (I'm trying to remember if she ever got statted up in the books, and what spells she knew. Considering that statted characters were not generally that strong, I'd bet on Celestial).<br /> <br /> Now, in the future, sure, some Solar (maybe your PC!) will rediscover the ancient lost secrets of the Adamant Circle (perhaps after battling Raksi in a mighty sorcerous duel to claim the Book of Three Circles, or maybe by completing a mighty quest to find the hidden Heart of Adamant in the temple of Zel-Run, or by outwitting the demon prince Koraneth in a battle of wits, forcing him to give up his secrets... or maybe just developing it by yourself because your party isn't interested in these quests*), and become the most powerful sorcerer in all of Creation, but that hasn't happened yet, because no Solar has yet reached Essence 5.<br /> <br /> *I admit, I didn't make either of the PCs who got Solar sorcery go on exciting quests, because the party was doing other things, but one did learn the spells from an ancient forbidden god.<br /> <br /> So, while Solars have the most sorcerous <i>potential</i>, the most powerful sorcerers in Creation in 768RY are almost certainly Lunar and Sidereal elders.<br /> (The most powerful sorcerer of all is probably a 3rd circle demon, but they don't live in Creation.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T06:50:14-07:00","id":1129205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1129199#post1129199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> a bit less than Sidereals (that's why I said there's probably 3-4 times as many Lunar sorcerers than Sidereals: there's 4 times as many Lunars, but there may not be 4 times as many Lunar sorcerers).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI feel as though there's a contradiction in this sentence, unless by &quot;there may not be 4 times as many Lunar sorcerers&quot;, you just mean &quot;there could 'just' be 3 times as many&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T06:57:51-07:00","id":1129207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1129205#post1129205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI feel as though there's a contradiction in this sentence, unless by &quot;there may not be 4 times as many Lunar sorcerers&quot;, you just mean &quot;there could 'just' be 3 times as many&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the lack of infrastructure for Lunars, while Sidereals have all of Yu Shan to work with, and the differences between Lunars and Sidereals themselves, I suspect that the Sidereals have the advantage in terms of sorcerer/non-sorcerer ratio. However, there are more Lunars, and so probably more Lunar sorcerers in absolute terms. I see no contradiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T07:33:02-07:00","id":1129220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1129200#post1129200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My point, is that in 768 RY probably not a single Exalt can cast spells from the Adamant Circle. Maybe, <i>maybe</i>, Samea. I think she's sometimes been depicted in the fluff as being able to. But I think generally, it's probably better for the setting that she's a Celestial sorcerer, which I think is how she's generally been shown.<br /> (I'm trying to remember if she ever got statted up in the books, and what spells she knew. Considering that statted characters were not generally that strong, I'd bet on Celestial).<br /> <br /> Now, in the future, sure, some Solar (maybe your PC!) will rediscover the ancient lost secrets of the Adamant Circle (perhaps after battling Raksi in a mighty sorcerous duel to claim the Book of Three Circles, or maybe by completing a mighty quest to find the hidden Heart of Adamant in the temple of Zel-Run, or by outwitting the demon prince Koraneth in a battle of wits, forcing him to give up his secrets... or maybe just developing it by yourself because your party isn't interested in these quests*), and become the most powerful sorcerer in all of Creation, but that hasn't happened yet, because no Solar has yet reached Essence 5.<br /> <br /> *I admit, I didn't make either of the PCs who got Solar sorcery go on exciting quests, because the party was doing other things, but one did learn the spells from an ancient forbidden god.<br /> <br /> So, while Solars have the most sorcerous <i>potential</i>, the most powerful sorcerers in Creation in 768RY are almost certainly Lunar and Sidereal elders.<br /> (The most powerful sorcerer of all is probably a 3rd circle demon, but they don't live in Creation.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, didn't think about it. You're right, <i>at the moment</i> Lunars should have the most accomplished sorcerers in Creation. In the future that will no longer be necessarily true, but, well, that's the thing with the future. Sidereals might have more, and better trained, but I doubt that. And Abyssals are probably still learning, and necromancy isn't as versatile as sorcery. Hypothetical Infernals are probably in similar conditions.<br /> <br /> It just occurred to me that probably the most powerful sorcerers in Creation, right now, are the Deathlords... but they're very few, they're not a splat, and they're not usually in Creation AFAIK. Also they would probably use necromancy too, leaving them at a disadvantage, I think (although I might very well be wrong).<br /> <br /> I still don't get why according to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a> Lunars were <i>the most powerful sorcerers in the 1st Age</i>... I mean, back then the Solars were generally at their most powerful, and their best sorcerers had mastery of all 3 circles. But perhaps there's some bit of canon I'm not familiar with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T07:51:14-07:00","id":1129226,"title":"","content":"The surviving First Age Lunars are the most powerful sorcerers in Creation right now (the Twilight Solars were during the High First Age). I mught be wrong, but I though that around one-third of Lunars are No Moons, so around one-half of Lunars probably possess Terrestrial and/or Celestial Circle Sorcery. All of the existing First Age Lunar Exalted should probably possess both, dozens of spells for each, and have created hundreds of surviving workings since the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> Oh, any word on the No Moon power yet? I would imagine that it would be 'spend one mote to reduce the sorcery mote cost of spells by one, up to twice Essence (or something)'. That would allow No Moons to chain spells more quickly than any other being in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T07:54:45-07:00","id":1129227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1129226#post1129226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, any word on the No Moon power yet? I would imagine that it would be 'spend one mote to reduce the sorcery mote cost of spells by one, up to twice Essence (or something)'. That would allow No Moons to chain spells more quickly than any other being in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds like a great reason not to have it then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> more seriously, No-Moons are presumably not all sorcerers, in the same way Twilights aren't all sorcerers. Their anima powers probably will be useful for sorcery, but I don't think any splat will directly effect sorcery as part of a passive-no-cost-power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T08:02:41-07:00","id":1129231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1129207#post1129207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see no contradiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I said there's probably 3-4 times as many Lunar sorcerers than Sidereals&quot; and &quot;there may not be 4 times as many Lunar sorcerers&quot; are saying the exact opposite things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T08:28:51-07:00","id":1129243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1129231#post1129231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;I said there's probably 3-4 times as many Lunar sorcerers than Sidereals&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;there may not be 4 times as many Lunar sorcerers&amp;quot; are saying the exact opposite things.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as 3-4 isn't inclusive, sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T08:44:20-07:00","id":1129248,"title":"","content":"I see what you mean, maybe it's not 100% clear.<br /> What I meant is, the most obvious answer to how many Lunar sorcerers there are compared to Sidereal sorcerers, is 4 times as many, because there's 4 times as many Lunars.<br /> But I said there's probably 3-4 times as many, rather than 4 times as many, because I reckon it's probably a little less. But I'm not sure, maybe it's the same proportion. As I said, I don't think it's necessary to put exact numbers on, so I went for something a bit vague.<br /> It could be, for example, that there are the same proportion of Sidereal and Lunar sorcerers (so 4 times... well, I guess actually it'd be more like 5 times, but anyway), but the Lunars on average know less spells, or something.<br /> <br /> I think there probably isn't only twice as many Lunar sorcerers, or as many as six times as many. I'd say 3-4 times as many, but maybe err towards 3. But as I said, it doesn't matter exactly.<br /> <br /> <br /> I hope that's a bit clearer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals might have more, and better trained, but I doubt that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I reckon they might, on average, be better trained, because they probably have a more unified and structured system of teaching sorcery, but considering there's 4 to 5 times as many Lunars as Sidereals, I imagine Lunar sorcerers would outnumber Sidereal sorcerers considerably, as I was saying to Isator.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The surviving First Age Lunars are the most powerful sorcerers in Creation right now (the Twilight Solars were during the High First Age).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so you meant the First Age Lunars are the most powerful sorcerers, rather than Lunars were the most powerful in the first age. Sure, that makes sense, though it's possible that the First Age Sidereal sorcerers* are more powerful.<br /> They're probably roughly the same, I'd think (and it probably works best, from the game perspective, to assume they're roughly the same).<br /> <br /> *I assume, in all of this talk of whose the most powerful sorcerer, we mean mechanically, like how many spells you know. Because, socially, people might consider evocations or powerful and bizarre charms to be part of a sorcerer's powers. I mean, in the Realm, being a sorcerer isn't about knowing 2-3 spells, it's about having demon servants and a magical tower where you plunder the eldritch secrets of the universe, and never being invited to parties (or maybe getting invitations with the social knowledge that you're expected to refuse, but the hosts don't have to explain why they didn't invite you).<br /> In which case the most powerful sorcerer is probably a Sidereal elder who not only knows plenty of celestial spells, but has far more artefacts than any of the Lunar celestial sorcerers. And brags about it. A lot.<br /> Hmmm... does having a bunch of Getimians work for you count as having magical servants? Does parrying the decrees of Saturn using forbidden techniques count as sorcery? I'm going to say no, but it's just something I thought worth mentioning.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mught be wrong, but I though that around one-third of Lunars are No Moons, so around one-half of Lunars probably possess Terrestrial and/or Celestial Circle Sorcery. All of the existing First Age Lunar Exalted should probably possess both, dozens of spells for each, and have created hundreds of surviving workings since the Usurpation.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot to say here, so I want to unpack it a bit (I hope it doesn't look nitpicky, I think there's just a lot to say).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but I though that around one-third of Lunars are No Moons </div> </div> </div>Not sure. It doesn't sound ridiculous. There could be a bit less, but that seems like an okay number. About a third for each caste seems reasonable (probably fluctuating a bit).<br /> Of course, in 2nd ed there was definitely a lot less than 1/3rd of Lunar PCs who were No Moons, but as they're one of my favourite castes, I hope to see them get a charmset that's actually as good as the Changing Moon and Full Moon charmset this edition!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> so around one-half of Lunars probably possess Terrestrial and/or Celestial Circle Sorcery </div> </div> </div>Okay, so there's two things here. First, I don't think we should assume all No Moons are sorcerers. It's pretty lame when No Moon players are supposed to be all about something that isn't part of the Lunar charmset anyway. And there's plenty of mental concepts that don't require being a sorcerer. You could be a genius hunter with a perfect awareness of your environment, a quick-witted trickster, a genius polymath who can turn their mind to any problem... being a sorcerer is something quite character-significant, and I don't think should be the default.<br /> It's also, in this edition, not something that's so easy to teach (I should know, my Owl-totem celestial sorcerer tried to teach his lazy, unfocused Fox-totem daughter a few times, and she just couldn't get it. Teenagers have no attention spans), so it's not like all No Moons can be forced through the five stations by their teachers.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, obviously they can get it (both the Full Moon and Casteless in the game I ran learnt it, the Full Moon had Celestial), which is why you said half might have it.<br /> <br /> But then we come to, well... just how many Exalts are sorcerers? Which is quite a good question.<br /> I mean, PC-wise, in my experience it's not common at the beginning (maybe 1 in 4?) but becomes more common as characters go on, and learn it from various sources. By the end of my game, 4 out of 7 characters had it.<br /> But is that just a PC thing, or something you could say more generally? Becoming a sorcerer is quite a significant character-building event... but obviously, for Lunars who've been around for a hundred years, that may well have happened to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All of the existing First Age Lunar Exalted should probably possess both </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. I think there'll be First Age Lunars who are all about brutal combat, or charm, and not about magical knowledge. I think it'll be common amongst Elders, but not every single one. And some will have Terrestrial but not Celestial, because it's just a small part of who they are.<br /> <br /> I've seen some very experienced Lunar PCs (I mean, essence 5, or 600+xp, etc) with Celestial sorcery and loads of spells, and others with just 1 or 2 spells. I imagine it'd be like that. They are individuals, after all. Some might have 100 combat charms and like 3 spells. Others, of course, will have loads of spells.<br /> <br /> I don't really see Tammuz or Lilith or Admiral Leviathan as having tons of celestial spells. It's just not their thing. But Lilith probably knows tons and tons of martial arts instead, because that's her thing IIRC (I might not, I never was that interested in her), not sorcery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> dozens of spells for each, and have created hundreds of surviving workings since the Usurpation. </div> </div> </div>Of those that are committed sorcerers (like Raksi), this seems pretty reasonable. And yeah, I'm sure there'll be tons and tons of workings. Maybe thousands, though that includes ones that aren't that important. Big significant ones (Celestial or Solar)... yeah, across the entirety of Creation, probably hundreds.<br /> Which gives STs plenty to work with, there's lots of interesting plots and societies you can do with left-over workings created by Lunar sorcerers in the past 1500 years, even before you get to the smaller number of ancient Lunar sorcerers who are still actually around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, any word on the No Moon power yet? I would imagine that it would be 'spend one mote to reduce the sorcery mote cost of spells by one, up to twice Essence (or something)'. That would allow No Moons to chain spells more quickly than any other being in Creation. </div> </div> </div>I hope not. Believe me, as someone who played a No Moon celestial sorcerer in both editions, it is actually a rubbish, rubbish, rubbish power.<br /> The +1 DV is way better.<br /> I must have played him in... oh, 70 games? Not sure. Well, let me tell you, I used the mote-reduction power in precisely one game. One. And it wasn't that useful, it just saved me 4 motes.<br /> The edition change, incidentally, has made it marginally better, but not good enough to be a good power. I guess it's not total weaksauce, it's probably about as good as a Night's ability to ignore Essence dots of penalties to stealth attempts. But it's certainly nowhere near the level of a caste's headline anima power (like, say, the Changing Moon's amazing ability to disguise themselves as whoever for a scene, which is so good that I hope they get something else instead so people don't try to find excuses to make their mental character a Changing Moon).<br /> <br /> I'd like <i>good</i> powers this edition. I'd also like to not have anima powers that say &quot;You are a combat sorcerer! Be a combat sorcerer! Why is your mental character not throwing multiple spells in a scene? What do you mean this is a social game?&quot; It in no way helps me with the spells I like casting, like Floral Ferry, Travel Without Distance, Shadows of the Ancient Past, Celestial Banishment, etc.<br /> (I mean, in theory it could help with Celestial Banishment, I guess, but it never actually did in practice. If I wanted to banish multiple first circles, I just used Celestial Banishment to banish the whole group with a roll, and if I was fighting multiple Second-Circles by myself, I'd probably just leg it. Celestial spells are too expensive to be throwing out 2 or 3 in one combat, even with a 4-mote reduction.)<br /> <br /> Ideally, I'd like 3 powers unrelated to sorcery (I heard everyone will get 3 powers, though that might be wrong), as I feel it dictates that all No Moons ought to be sorcerers, and if you're not then you're a rubbish No Moon (charms that affect sorcery are fine; if your No Moon isn't a sorcerer, you can not take them. Also I thought the sorcery charms for the example Lunar in the Core looked cool), but if I do get a sorcery-related anima power, I'd rather have something like &quot;You get Essence (minimum 3) sorcerous motes when you see the Moon, which last until the next Moonrise&quot;. You know, something I might use more than once in 80 games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-15-2017, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T10:26:57-07:00","id":1129290,"title":"","content":"I think that an appropriate alternative No Moon power would be allowing them to spend 5 motes of Essence to allow them to physically divide their brain for a scene so they could take two mental actions per turn without penalty. The Full Moon could have the same thing but for physical actions while the Changing Moons could have the same but for social actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T10:50:29-07:00","id":1129297,"title":"","content":"Samea closed a shadowland with a Solar Circle spell, didn't she? Or is that not canon anymore? If so, she may be the one living exalt who can cast such spells, but it's still possible someone like Raksi might have her beat in breadth of knowledge and number of Solar Circle workings accomplished, even if she can't call up a third circle demon in the course of a single night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T11:59:06-07:00","id":1129341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1129290#post1129290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that an appropriate alternative No Moon power would be allowing them to spend 5 motes of Essence to allow them to physically divide their brain for a scene so they could take two mental actions per turn without penalty. The Full Moon could have the same thing but for physical actions while the Changing Moons could have the same but for social actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tbh, those are extremely varied powers in power level. And No Moons are still getting the raw end of the deal. I want No Moon powers that are as good as Full Moon or Changing Moon powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> I had a go at making my own Lunar 3rd ed conversion once (I got bored about a third of the way through). It seemed easy to use equivalents across the 3 castes with different Attributes, like you have (for example, I gave them the ability to reset a charm of the appropriate attribute once per day), but I realised later that there's no real need to use similar powers with different Attributes; it's just not that exciting. Also, they're not always very equivalent, for various reasons, as you are more likely to want to use some charms repeatedly.<br /> <br /> I think the current Devs can probably come up with much more creative things than just bonuses using the attribute (though I would be okay with one or two powers that are something like reset or ignore penalties for your attributes, like you suggested; if they've got 3 anima powers each, they don't all have to be super-exciting).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Samea closed a shadowland with a Solar Circle spell, didn't she? Or is that not canon anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>I also remember that, but it was just in a chapter story, and I don't think those were canon. This is why I'm not sure if she's supposed to be or not. So yeah, if there's anyone in the setting who can cast Solar spells, it's Samea (she has been a sorcerer longer than any other Solar, after all, but still only like 10 or 20 years, which isn't long unless you're a PC). But I wouldn't say she definitely can (and I personally would say she can't; I'd prefer to let a PC rediscover Solar sorcery. But if I did want to have a Solar sorcerer NPC in a game set in a North, I'd probably use her).<br /> <br /> Of course, I think closing a shadowland is a working now, rather than a spell, so she wouldn't need to be a Solar sorcerer to do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">someone like Raksi might have her beat in breadth of knowledge and number of Solar Circle workings accomplished, even if she can't call up a third circle demon in the course of a single night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, while Raksi may not have Solar sorcery, she probably knows tons and tons of Celestial spells, and may well have cast several Solar workings (and lots of lower-level ones) over her life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T12:46:11-07:00","id":1129366,"title":"","content":"With 1500 years of time and Celestial Circle Sorcery, I think that Raksi could have easily completed around one Solar Working every century without it taking up too much of her time (we will know more about the exact capabilities of Lunar sorcerers when the book comes out in 2018). Celestial and Terrestrial Workings would be fairly trivial exercises for her, so she might have done one every decade and every year respectively without them taking up too much of her time. That would mean that she could have easily accomplished, for example, 15 Ambition 1 Solar Workings, 150 Ambition 2 Celestial Workings, and 1500 Ambition 3 Terrestrial Workings over the last 1,500 years, which would make me highly reluctant to attack her base of operations (an Ambition 1 Solar Working could easily make a city into a supernatural death trap).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T13:07:25-07:00","id":1129379,"title":"","content":"To be honest, when I thought about it, I just wasn't sure there would be a dozen plus Solar workings that she would have wanted to make (at least, ones that are still relevant: she might have moved her friend's soul into an immortal golem 800 years ago, and since then the golem went and lived somewhere else, or something like that). But if she wanted to, it's certainly doable.<br /> <br /> But yeah, attacking Rathess could be really, really nasty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T13:15:31-07:00","id":1129384,"title":"","content":"I think you mean Mahalanka, Rathess is a former Dragon King City.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T14:03:05-07:00","id":1129414,"title":"","content":"Oops, yes I do. I get the names confused because they're both ancient cities of ancient stuff in the east-south-eastern jungles.<br /> And the playgroup I used to play with would invade either Rathess or Mahalanka pretty often in different games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T19:40:51-07:00","id":1130092,"title":"","content":"I've no doubt that Raksi, as learned and powerful as she is, COULD pop out an Adamant Working.<br /> <br /> The question is if she WOULD. Raksi is a reclusive academic. It's possible that her last Working was something to ward Raksha away from her city because the Balorian Crusade happened and the noise kept her from studying","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T02:53:32-07:00","id":1130191,"title":"","content":"I believe that prior Editions didn't have her take up in Mahalanka until after the Contagion, and I would maintain that.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy image of her still has her engaging in all kinds of sorcerous experiments, so she still would have used the occasional Adamant working to horrific effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T06:29:33-07:00","id":1130229,"title":"","content":"And I do not think that one Solar Working a century would be too much for someone of her capabilities. Of course, only one or two of them might have been Ambition 3, but they would have still been impressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:22:40-07:00","id":1130401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1127764-great-news-for-lunar-fans?p=1130191#post1130191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bMy image of her still has her engaging in all kinds of sorcerous experiments, so she still would have used the occasional Adamant working to horrific effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I could quote psychologists of learning, but essentially, practical learning involves <i>doing</i>, not just reading books. And sorcery is a very practical form of knowledge.<br /> <br /> I'm sure she's done all sorts of bizarre workings to see what happens, and to improve her skills, including Adamant workings.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}